text:
D.A. Wallach’s Theory: The real bubble is in “safe” stocks

@dawallach: “It’s a desire to pretend that you are intrepid and innovative and love technology and are driving the future without taking risk.”

“Walmart and Costco are trading at price-to-earnings ratios today of 40 or 50. And NVIDIA is trading at 16”

@davemcclure: “As switching costs go down, the durability of future cash flows also goes down.”

